    {
      "id": "3d4f36fd36abe86859f67c4945ddcdf5b66c7637",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 455728804,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Can someone more experienced with pipes look this over to see if it properly resolves the issue?\n\nThe complication here is that since the `pipename` can also be a socket, it might not be possible to remove the first call to `stat`",
          "author": {
            "id": 3194989,
            "username": "moshekaplan",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Moshe Kaplan",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/3194989/avatar.png?v=1789950604",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/moshekaplan"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-11-26T20:09:36.910Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-11-26T20:28:16.367Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 79700692,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1045,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4d1150294a84bd68fe2727ac53f33bf4618bab42",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 455792678,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> The complication here is that since the `pipename` can also be a socket, it might not be possible to remove the first call to `stat`\n\nTo quote [the Single UNIX Specification page for `open()`](https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/functions/open.html):\n\n> These functions may fail if:\n> \n>   ...\n> \n> [EOPNOTSUPP]\\\n>   The *path* argument names a socket.\n\nSo there is no guarantee that an `open()` will succeed on a UNIX-domain socket, and you'll have to either:\n\n1. do the first `stat()`;\n1. try to open it and, if you get `EOPNOTSUPP`, try to connect to it;\n\nor something such as that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-11-26T20:56:53.201Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-11-26T20:56:53.201Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 79700692,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
