    {
      "id": "01884edc9cd4a0ce866510956955a34dd744b507",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 910918522,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The comment Coverity provides for that issue is\n\n> In cap_pipe_open_live: A check occurs on a file's attributes before the file is used in a privileged operation, but things may have changed (CWE-367)\n\nThe file should, ideally, not be used in a privileged operation *even if it's a named pipe* - the only stuff we should do, before giving up privileges, is opening capture devices.\n\nWhat I guess we could do, if we want to avoid doing stat-and-then-open, is try to open it and:\n\n- if the open succeeds check to see whether it's a pipe or a socket, in which case we continue, or something else, in which case we fail;\n- if the open fails with `EOPNOTSUPP` (macOS, possibly other BSD-flavored OSes), `ENXIO` (Linux), or perhaps other errors (AIX, Solaris, HP-UX, possibly other BSD-flavored OSes), try to connect to it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-04-13T06:55:33.128Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-04-13T06:55:33.128Z",
